{
 "info": {
  "name": "Fund Management System v1",
  "description": "The money surface of a broking account. Seven endpoints under /api/v1/funds.\n\nSet the `baseUrl`, `username` and `password` collection variables before running anything. Every request inherits HTTP Basic auth from the collection, so no request carries its own Authorization header.\n\n**On the scheme.** Basic is what the service enforces today, and it is provisional — see `platformAuth` in openapi.json and the note at `ApiSecurityConfiguration.httpBasic`. This collection previously sent a bearer token, which the service does not accept, so every request answered 401. When the platform gateway's token issuer is settled the credential becomes a bearer token; until then a bearer value authenticates nothing here.\n\nTwo conventions hold everywhere:\n\n- **Money is an integer count of paise.** `{\"paise\": 12345, \"currency\": \"INR\"}` is ₹123.45. A decimal or a quoted number is refused with 400, not truncated.\n- **Errors are branched on by `code`, never by `message`.** The message is a developer-facing explanation and is not stable.\n\nFull reference: docs/api/README.md",
  "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
 },
 "auth": {
  "type": "basic",
  "basic": [
   {
    "key": "username",
    "value": "{{username}}",
    "type": "string"
   },
   {
    "key": "password",
    "value": "{{password}}",
    "type": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "variable": [
  {
   "key": "baseUrl",
   "value": "http://localhost:8080",
   "type": "string",
   "description": "Host and port only, no context path. The service has none."
  },
  {
   "key": "username",
   "value": "",
   "type": "string",
   "description": "The account's UCC. It is the authenticated subject, and every endpoint resolves the account from it — no request body or path carries an account identifier."
  },
  {
   "key": "password",
   "value": "",
   "type": "string",
   "description": "The credential for that subject. Provisional scheme: see the collection description. A gateway ahead of the service may reject the request before it arrives, with the gateway's error shape rather than this service's."
  },
  {
   "key": "requestId",
   "value": "0",
   "type": "string",
   "description": "Captured automatically from the POST /payout response. The default is 0 so the path stays well-formed when there is no open request; a 64-bit id that cannot exist answers 409 with reason NOT_FOUND, which is the endpoint's own refusal rather than a routing miss."
  },
  {
   "key": "reference",
   "value": "FMS-NO-SUCH-ENTRY",
   "type": "string",
   "description": "Captured automatically from the first entry of GET /transactions. The default is deliberately a reference that cannot exist: with an empty period there is nothing to capture, and an EMPTY variable collapsed the URL to /transactions/ — an unmapped path whose 404 carries a body, so the request tested Spring's routing instead of this endpoint."
  }
 ],
 "item": [
  {
   "name": "Withdrawals",
   "description": "Requesting and cancelling withdrawals. A request reserves nothing: it settles at end of day against whatever is available then, which is why every response carries a shrink warning key.",
   "item": [
    {
     "name": "Request a withdrawal",
     "event": [
      {
       "listen": "test",
       "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
         "// Capture the id so the cancel request below works without editing a variable.",
         "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
         "    const body = pm.response.json();",
         "    pm.collectionVariables.set('requestId', String(body.requestId));",
         "",
         "    pm.test('paise is an integer', () =>",
         "        pm.expect(Number.isInteger(body.withdrawableAtRequest.paise)).to.be.true);",
         "    pm.test('the shrink warning is present', () =>",
         "        pm.expect(body.shrinkWarningKey).to.eql('WITHDRAWAL_MAY_SHRINK_AT_SETTLEMENT'));",
         "    pm.test('the destination is masked', () =>",
         "        pm.expect(body.destinationMasked).to.not.match(/\\d{9,}/));",
         "} else {",
         "    // Every refusal on this path is branched on by code, so surface it.",
         "    console.log('refused:', pm.response.json().code, pm.response.json().details);",
         "}"
        ]
       }
      }
     ],
     "request": {
      "method": "POST",
      "header": [
       {
        "key": "Content-Type",
        "value": "application/json"
       }
      ],
      "body": {
       "mode": "raw",
       "raw": "{\n  \"amount\": {\n    \"paise\": 500000,\n    \"currency\": \"INR\"\n  },\n  \"destinationRef\": \"acc-4471\"\n}",
       "options": {
        "raw": {
         "language": "json"
        }
       }
      },
      "url": {
       "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/funds/payout",
       "host": [
        "{{baseUrl}}"
       ],
       "path": [
        "api",
        "v1",
        "funds",
        "payout"
       ]
      },
      "description": "Creates the account's single open withdrawal request.\n\nNo account identifier anywhere in the body: the account comes from the token's subject claim.\n\nOne open request per account, enforced by a partial unique index rather than by a service check. A second request while one is open returns 409 `request_already_open`. Do not build a check-then-submit flow around this; handle the 409.\n\n**Failures**\n\n- 400 `invalid_request` — malformed body, missing field, decimal paise\n- 409 `request_already_open` / `withdrawable_unavailable` / `figures_stale`\n- 422 `amount_exceeds_withdrawable` (details carry `requested` and `withdrawable`) / `destination_not_verified`\n- 503 `upstream_unavailable` / `calendar_unavailable`"
     },
     "response": [
      {
       "name": "201 Created",
