  {
   "name": "Transactions",
   "description": "History in either of two views, and its CSV export.\n\nMOVEMENTS carries only money the trader moved in or out. ALL_ENTRIES carries every entry with its running balance. Sale proceeds and charges are not payins and never appear in MOVEMENTS.",
   "item": [
    {
     "name": "History — MOVEMENTS (default 30 days)",
     "event": [
      {
       "listen": "test",
       "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
         "const body = pm.response.json();",
         "if (body.entries.length > 0) {",
         "    pm.collectionVariables.set('reference', body.entries[0].reference);",
         "}",
         "// Rule L7: an empty period comes back with the period echoed and a wider one",
         "// suggested, never a bare empty array.",
         "pm.test('an empty period suggests a wider one', () => {",
         "    if (body.entries.length === 0) {",
         "        pm.expect(body.suggestedWiderPeriod).to.not.be.null;",
         "    }",
         "});",
         "pm.test('the period is echoed back', () =>",
         "    pm.expect(body.period).to.have.keys('from', 'to'));"
        ]
       }
      }
     ],
     "request": {
      "method": "GET",
      "header": [],
      "url": {
       "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/funds/transactions",
       "host": [
        "{{baseUrl}}"
       ],
       "path": [
        "api",
        "v1",
        "funds",
        "transactions"
       ],
       "query": [
        {
         "key": "view",
         "value": "MOVEMENTS",
         "disabled": true,
         "description": "MOVEMENTS or ALL_ENTRIES. Defaults to MOVEMENTS."
        },
        {
         "key": "from",
         "value": "2026-07-23",
         "disabled": true,
         "description": "Inclusive. Send both bounds or neither — one alone is treated as none."
        },
        {
         "key": "to",
         "value": "2026-08-21",
         "disabled": true,
         "description": "Inclusive. The window may not exceed 92 days."
        }
       ]
      },
      "description": "Omit both bounds for the 30-day default. The number is not a round-figure guess: the mandated return of unused funds runs monthly or quarterly and is among the most-queried entries, so a shorter default shows an empty table for a transaction the trader knows happened.\n\nNo pagination, here or upstream — the back office's ledger endpoint has no offset, no cursor and no row limit, so the 92-day window is the only bound on response size. A wider range is walked in windows by the caller.\n\nThe response echoes the period actually used. Render from that rather than from what you asked for."
     },
